WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.092
Use this checkpoint to connect business questions with SQL patterns.

00:00:04.092 --> 00:00:09.862
Named stages suggest CTEs. Hierarchies suggest recursion.

00:00:09.862 --> 00:00:14.062
Group context beside detail suggests window functions.

00:00:14.062 --> 00:00:20.182
Previous-event questions suggest LAG. Top N per group suggests ranking in one stage and filtering in another.

00:00:20.182 --> 00:00:25.332
The pattern choice should follow the analytical question.

00:00:25.332 --> 00:00:29.797
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:29.797 --> 00:00:32.972
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:32.972 --> 00:00:38.977
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:38.977 --> 00:00:43.642
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:50.447
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:50.447 --> 00:00:54.432
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project:

00:00:54.432 --> 00:00:59.040
validate the meaning of the result, not only whether the statement executes.
